    "show_share": true,
    "description": "For most graduate, the instant transition from nursing school to hospital as Trainee Nurse Interns (TNI) is an exciting and yet a stressful event in their life. They are suddenly taken away from the protecting and nurturing umbrella of the school and burdened by increased clinical responsibilities where their actions could have severe consequences. On top of that it is expected that they are well-equipped with knowledge, critical thinking and dexterity to succeed in their work. This sudden change, sometimes creates source of low confidence and pressure for the TNIs, thus a skill refresher is needed to mitigate the anxiety and alleviate some pressure.",
